#. translators: This string is injected verbatim into LLM system prompts via the UCP manifest. Translate the natural-language prose, but DO NOT translate the technical identifiers (`requires_escalation`, `continue_url`, `/checkout-sessions`, `unsupported_operation`, `UCP-Agent`, `Product/Version`, `Other AI`, `RFC 8941`) or HTTP methods (POST, GET, PUT, PATCH, DELETE) — agents must see these tokens exactly. The two header examples must be copied character for character, including the straight ASCII double quotes around the URL: UCP-Agent: profile="https://your-agent.example/profile" and UCP-Agent: YourAgent/1.0. Do NOT substitute locale-appropriate smart or angled quotes — the store parses that header with a regex requiring literal ASCII quotes, so a typographic substitution would tell agents to send a header that does not work.
#: includes/ai-storefront/class-wc-ai-storefront-ucp.php:716
msgid "This store uses requires_escalation checkout: agents do not place orders directly. POST /checkout-sessions returns a continue_url with attribution UTMs already attached; redirect the user to that URL to complete the purchase on the merchant site. The /checkout-sessions/{id} URL is stateless — GET, PUT, PATCH, and DELETE all return HTTP 405 with code \"unsupported_operation\" because there is no persistent session to act on. Send your agent identity via the UCP-Agent header so attribution canonicalizes to your brand rather than bucketing as \"Other AI\". Preferred form, per RFC 8941: UCP-Agent: profile=\"https://your-agent.example/profile\". Product/Version form (UCP-Agent: YourAgent/1.0) is also accepted. Near-miss spellings of the profile form — colon-delimited, unquoted, or a bare URL as the whole header value — are parsed too, but the quoted form is the one to send."
msgstr ""

